<title>USA: Fed approves powers for BOK Financial.</title>
<headline>Fed approves powers for BOK Financial.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve said on Monday it had given its approval for BOK Financial Corp of Tulsa, Okla, to engage through a subsidiary in underwriting and dealing in municipal revenue bonds, commercial paper and consumer receivable-related securities.</p>
<p>BOK Financial, with total assets of $4.5 billion, is the largest bank in Oklahoma and the 94th largest bank in the United States. It operates banks in Oklahoma, Texas and Arkansas.</p>
</text>
